        "parms": "# ~saw — a bright oscillator\nA ~saw plays a sawtooth wave: a ramp up and a drop, every harmonic of its pitch at once, so it sounds bright and buzzy. Since libYSE 3.0 it swings from -1 to 1 around 0, like ~sine. Its argument is the frequency in Hz, 440 by default.\nMax's saw~ has a second inlet to sync its phase; ~saw has only the frequency inlet. Like ~sine, it takes the frequency as a float: an int is ignored.",
